  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Lightly score edges of steak at 1-inch intervals. Preheat grill or broiler.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine butter, parsley, onion, Worcestershire sauce, pepper and mustard in a small saucepan. Heat, stirring continually, over low heat, until butter melts. Reserve 1/2 of the mixture.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Place steak on grill or broiler pan. Brush steak with butter mixture. Cook, basting frequently with butter mixture, about 6 minutes per side for medium.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Place steak on a serving platter. Cut thin slices across the grain. Drizzle reserved butter mixture over steak.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [
    "Tip: it's easy to please individual tastes by grilling or broiling steaks to-order. Cut steak into serving-size portions before cooking.",
    "Tip: a clean grill rack helps prevent meat from sticking. Rub a wire brush over the rack after the grill has been sufficiently heated."
  ],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "Make ahead: leftover steak keeps well wrapped in the refrigerator for up to 2 days. Slice and serve alongside eggs or make a hearty last-minute salad for a weeknight supper."
    },
    {
      "text": "Variation: sprinkle fresh herbs on hot coals while grilling to enhance the flavor of the meat."
